 PCM integration – status

  We've connected ServiceNow to the PCM cashflow API using svcnewsd and built a reusable client.

  Working — retrieving live data via the MID server in ~700ms. Filters work precisely: an exact amount + date returns
  exactly the right cashflow. Request contract confirmed (all seven criteria mandatory, Amount as a magnitude with
  Direction carrying the side).

  Blocker — CounterpartyName is mandatory, but in dev it's masked (CP Name (8577922)). A settlement email gives us the
  real name, never that token, so we can't yet query from an actual email. Counterparty Reference was the obvious
  fallback but is blank on 4 of 6 rows.

  Questions

  1. Is the data unmasked in UAT/prod? (most important — if yes, this is dev-only)
  2. Is there a lookup from a real counterparty name to that masked ID?
  3. Could CounterpartyName be optional or accept a wildcard? The other six criteria already narrow to one row.
  4. Is there a bulk variant? Currently one call per cashflow — ~290 cashflows, ~290 round trips.
  5. What does CaseNumber represent?
  6. Any update on the write-back API?
